T95-A-AV-R evidence — 2026-10-28 (card t_c81a4bad)

Everything below is raw output from a throwaway instrumentation run; the instrumentation was
reverted before any commit (`git checkout -- Mattermost/`). It exists so §1 of
docs/t95a-av2-build-note.md can be re-checked instead of believed.

How the instrumentation was produced (throwaway, NOT part of the deliverable):

  1. A file-writing probe helper appended to Mattermost/UI/Native/Sidebar/ChannelSidebarCoordinator.swift:

       /// THROWAWAY (T95-A-AV-R diagnosis only): append a line to a file the host can read.
       func t95probeFile(_ line: String) {
           let path = "/tmp/t95probe-parent.log"      // …-main.log in the second run
           guard let data = (line + "\n").data(using: .utf8) else { return }
           if let handle = FileHandle(forWritingAtPath: path) {
               handle.seekToEndOfFile(); handle.write(data); handle.closeFile()
           } else {
               try? data.write(to: URL(fileURLWithPath: path))
           }
       }

  2. Three call sites in applyLaunchDestinationIfNeeded(for:model:), at the top and at each guard:

       t95probeFile("T95PROBE decide enter opensDest=\(location.opensADestination) … groups=\(model.groups.count) phase=\(String(describing: model.phase))")
       guard !location.opensADestination else { t95probeFile("T95PROBE decide STOP opensDest"); return }
       if let current = location.serverID, current != server.id { t95probeFile("… STOP otherServer"); return }
       guard let teamID = model.teamID ?? location.teamID else { t95probeFile("… STOP noTeam"); return }
       // …and at the request guard / after openChannel:
       … else { t95probeFile("… STOP noRequest"); return }
       t95probeFile("… OPEN request=… outcome=…")

  3. On main only, one extra line at the top of the `model.$groups` sink in `model(for:)`:

       t95probeFile("T95PROBE sink groups=\(groups.count) self=\(self != nil) model=\(model != nil)")

  4. Probe test (also throwaway): launched the shell with
     `-uiTestResetPersistedState -uiTestForgetSession <url> -uiTestSeedServer <url> …`,
     signed in, then sampled tab bar / nativeChannelPane / `channelSidebar.channel.*` rows every
     250 ms for 75–90 s and printed every state change as `PROBE t=…`.

  Commands (fixture credentials come from the environment, never from a file):
     python3 bin/run_uitest.py --worktree <wt> --label t95av2-probe-parent6 \
       --only-testing MattermostUITests/T95ProbeUITests --sim id=614CEE50-… \
       --derived-data ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/t95av2-parent
     (bin/run_uitest.py wraps scripts/qa-test.py and sets TEST_RUNNER_MM_AUTH_* from the one password
      literal in scripts/*.py that actually logs in — several are stale on this fixture)

