Reading: six decide calls in the whole run, every one with `groups=0`. The channel list is on screen
11 rows at t=1.26 s in the same run (probe output below), so the directory *is* loaded — the decide
just never sees it. The parent's town-hall branch needs `hasTownHall` / `fallbackChannelID`, both
derived from `entries` (i.e. `groups`), so it answers `nil` at every launch decide: `STOP noRequest`.

