T95PROBE decide STOP opensDest

Reading: `sink groups=2` is immediately followed by `decide enter … groups=0` — `@Published`
publishes in **willSet**, so the decide triggered by the directory arriving reads the *previous*
(empty) value. A second decide, entered from the location-change path, does read `groups=2`; with
nothing saved `LaunchDestination.request` returns `nil` there by design (`-> none`), which is why
main is green. The reinstated-fallback mutant (§1 of the build note) hooks exactly that second decide
and reds the new assertion at 0.1 s.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§C  What is NOT evidence here
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* The 2026-10-27 AV pass (t_3a33a5ff) reported the parent UI test green twice and concluded the push
  "lands outside the 5 s window". §A shows the push does not land at all on that tree: the decide
  never reads a loaded directory. The parent commit is therefore not a red fixture for the UI test;
  the reinstated fallback is (build note §1).
* SwiftUI behaviour recorded while hunting the D1 mutation (build note §2): a `NavigationStack`
  placed inside the tab, with or without `.toolbar(.visible, for: .tabBar)` on the pushed
  destination, still hides the tab bar on iOS 18.3 — both mutants stayed green. Only a destination
  that itself carries a tab container renders a tab bar next to the pane, and that one reds
  `app.tabBars.count == 0`.
